url: 'https://github.com/Oluwaseun-O-Ajayi/SDL Framework'
abstract: >-
  SDL Framework is an open-source Python framework for
  closed-loop experimental optimization using self-driving
  laboratory principles. The framework provides reusable
  components for experiment representation, Bayesian
  optimization, acquisition-function-guided experiment
  selection, campaign orchestration, and workflow simulation.
  Example implementations demonstrate how adaptive
  optimization workflows can be modeled, analyzed, and
  reproduced within a transparent computational environment.
  The framework is intended for education, prototyping,
  and reproducibility-focused research involving
  self-driving laboratory concepts.
